.TP
.B [Rendering Resolution]:{Grid Rendering Resolution}==Medium Resolution Dimension==
.TP
.B [Rendering Resolution]:{Grid Rendering Resolution}==Low Resolution Dimension==
These set the largest number of grid cells drawn along each side of the
grid at medium and low resolution (rounded to multiples of 25; the low
resolution dimension is no larger than the medium one).
.TP
.B [Rendering Resolution]:{Nav Rendering Decimation}==Medium Resolution Decimation==
.TP
.B [Rendering Resolution]:{Nav Rendering Decimation}==Low Resolution Decimation==
These set the decimation (every nth point) of the navigation and vector data
drawn at medium and low resolution. Like routes, GIS polylines and polygons
are always drawn at full resolution.
.TP
.B [Rendering Resolution]:<Dismiss>
