.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS: MBview Site List Window
.TP
.B [Site List]:|Site List|
This list shows each site with its number, longitude, latitude, depth,
color, size, and name. Selecting a site highlights it in the displays;
clicking the selected site a second time changes its color to the next color
(skipping red, which marks the selection). Several sites can be selected with
the shift and control keys.
.TP
.B [Site List]:<Delete Selected Sites>
This button deletes the selected sites.
.TP
.B [Site List]:<Dismiss>
This button closes the list window.

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS: MBview Route List Window
.TP
.B [Route List]:|Route List|
This list shows each route, with its number, editability, number of
waypoints, length in plan view and along the topography, color, and name,
followed by its waypoints with their longitude, latitude, depth, distances
along the route, and waypoint type. Selecting a route or waypoint highlights
it in the displays. Clicking a selected route a second time changes its
color; clicking a selected waypoint a second time changes its waypoint type
(simple, transit, or start or end of a survey line of types 1 to 5).
.TP
.B [Route List]:<Delete Selected Routes>
This button deletes the selected routes and waypoints.
.TP
.B [Route List]:<Convert Selected to Polylines>
This button, present only when GIS polylines are displayed, converts each
selected route (selecting a route or any of its waypoints selects the route)
to a polyline through its waypoints, with the route's color, size, and name
and the topography at the waypoints. The polylines are placed in a layer named
"Converted from routes"; the routes are kept.
.TP
.B [Route List]:<Dismiss>
This button closes the list window.

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS: MBview Navigation List Window
.TP
.B [Navigation List]:|Navigation List|
This list shows each navigation file with its number, number of points,
color, size, and name. Selecting files selects all of their navigation, as
with the <Mouse->Select Nav File> mouse mode, and the profile follows the
selected navigation.
.TP
.B [Navigation List]:<Delete Selected Navigation>
This button deletes the selected navigation files from the display.
.TP
.B [Navigation List]:<Dismiss>
This button closes the list window.

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS: MBview Profile Window
.TP
.B [Profile]:|Profile|
The profile window shows the topography along the current two point pick,
selected route, or selected navigation, with the source, length, and depth
range above the plot. Segments steeper than the slope threshold are drawn in
red, and the boundaries between route or pick segments in green.
.TP
.B [Profile]:==Display Width Multiple==
This sets the width of the plot as a multiple (1 to 5) of the window width.
.TP
.B [Profile]:==Slope Threshold==
This sets the slope (from 0.01 to 2.00) above which segments are drawn in red.
.TP
.B [Profile]:==Vertical exaggeration==
This sets the vertical exaggeration of the profile.
.TP
.B [Profile]:<Dismiss>
This button closes the profile window.

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS: Generate Survey Route Window
This dialog, opened with <Action->Generate Survey Route from Area>, generates
a route of parallel survey lines covering the current area, run back and
forth along the length of the area, optionally with crosslines. Each line end
is a waypoint of type "start line". The route is generated when
\fBGenerate Route\fP is pressed; pressing it again with the same route name
replaces the route. The "Current Area Info" shows the area dimensions and the
resulting route.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Route Name"
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Route Color"
These set the name (default "Survey") and color of the route.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Line Spacing Mode"
This selects uniform line spacing or line spacing varying with the swath width
of the sonar.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Line Spacing (m)"
This sets the spacing of the lines in the uniform mode.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Platform Type"
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Swath Width (degrees)"
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Sonar Depth (m)"
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Sonar Altitude (m)"
In the variable mode these set whether the sonar is on a surface vessel, a
submerged vehicle at constant altitude, or a submerged vehicle at constant
depth, the sonar swath width, and the sonar depth or altitude. For constant
altitude the line spacing follows from the altitude and swath width; otherwise
each line spacing is calculated from the shallowest topography along the
previous line.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Start Corner"
This sets the corner of the area (SW, SE, NW, or NE) where the survey starts.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Interleaving"
This sets the number of passes over the area; with values greater than 1 the
lines are run in interleaved passes.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Cross Lines"
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:"Crosslines Before/After Survey"
These set the number of crosslines across the survey lines and whether they
are run before or after the survey lines.
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:<Generate Route>
.TP
.B [Survey Route]:<Dismiss>
These buttons generate the route and close the dialog.

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS: MBview Polyline, Polygon, and Point List Windows
.TP
.B [Polyline List]:|Polyline List|
.TP
.B [Polygon List]:|Polygon List|
.TP
.B [Point List]:|Point List|
These lists show each layer of the type, followed by its features. A layer
item shows whether the layer is shown or hidden, the number of features, and
the layer name; a feature item shows whether it is shown or hidden, its color,
its number of points and parts or rings (or for points the position and z
value), and its name. Selecting a single feature highlights it in red in the
displays. Clicking an item a second time changes its color to the next color
(skipping red); clicking a layer item a second time changes the color of all of
its features. Several items can be selected with the shift and control keys.
.TP
.B [Polyline List]:<Show/Hide Selected>
.TP
.B [Polygon List]:<Show/Hide Selected>
.TP
.B [Point List]:<Show/Hide Selected>
This button hides the selected features and layers if they are shown, or shows
them if they are hidden. Hidden features are still saved and exported.
.TP
.B [Polyline List]:<Delete Selected>
.TP
.B [Polygon List]:<Delete Selected>
.TP
.B [Point List]:<Delete Selected>
This button deletes the selected features; selecting a layer selects all of its
features.
.TP
.B [Polyline List]:<Convert Selected to Routes>
This button converts each part of each selected polyline (or of all polylines of
a selected layer) to an editable route with a waypoint at each vertex, keeping
the polyline's color, size, and name (with " part n" added for polylines with
several parts). Vertices that cannot be placed in the display are not used, and
their number is printed to the terminal. The polylines are kept.
.TP
.B [Polyline List]:<Dismiss>
.TP
.B [Polygon List]:<Dismiss>
.TP
.B [Point List]:<Dismiss>
